{"build":"d2d3291@22/11/2026, 17:23:59","data":{"book":{"title":"Pocket Kirtan Guide","subtitle":"Nabadwip, 2013","slug":"en-pe","language":"en","sort_order":8,"is_legacy":{"show_micro_thumbnail_on_main":true},"songsCount":80},"descriptions":[{"title":"Kirtan Guide","title_full_short":"Kīrtan Guide 12th Ed","subtitle":"London, Twelfth Edition, 2026","slug":"en","sort_order":1,"shortcuts":[{"icon":"clock","title":"The Daily Programme","slug":"003-programme"}],"audio":{"filter":{"by_title":["Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Srila B.R. Sridhar Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Nabadwip temple","Kamal Krishna Prabhu","Manasa Krishna Prabhu"]}},"songsCount":194},{"title":"Гаудия Гитанджали","subtitle":"Cборник вайшнавских песен и молитв","slug":"ru","sort_order":2,"render":{"tg.contents.first_line":false,"tg.a-z.title.words":3},"songsCount":178},{"title":"Guía de Kīrtan","subtitle":"Edición Detallada. Con traducción palabra por palabra y explicación de estilo","slug":"es","sort_order":3,"songsCount":146},{"title":"Livro de Kirtan","subtitle":"Seva Ashram, Campos do Jordão","slug":"pt","language":"pt-BR","sort_order":4,"songsCount":112},{"title":"Ґаудія Ґітанджалі","subtitle":"Вайшнавський пісенник українскою мовою","slug":"ua","sort_order":6,"language":"uk","render":{"tg.contents.first_line":false,"tg.a-z.title.words":4},"songsCount":74},{"title":"Kirtan Guide","subtitle":"Chiang Mai English Edition, 2022","slug":"en-2022","sort_order":7,"hidden":false,"is_legacy":{"show_micro_thumbnail_on_main":true},"songsCount":166},{"title":"Pocket Kirtan Guide","subtitle":"Nabadwip, 2013","slug":"en-pe","language":"en","sort_order":8,"is_legacy":{"show_micro_thumbnail_on_main":true},"songsCount":80}],"nav":{"100":{"prev":{"path":"/en-pe/he-deva-bhavantam-vande/","title":"He deva bhavantaṁ vande"},"next":{"path":"/en-pe/jaya-jaya-radha-krishna-jugala-milan/","title":"Śrī Vraja-dhāma-mahimāmṛta"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":100,"first_line":"janama saphala tā’ra","author":"Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"},"title":["Rūpa-Kīrtan"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["janama saphala tā’ra    kṛṣṇa-daraśana yā’ra","    bhāgye ha-iyāchhe eka-bāra","vikaśiyā hṛn-nayana    kari’ kṛṣṇa daraśana","    chhāḍe jīva chitera vikāra"],"translation":["The birth of one who, by good fortune, has once seen Kṛṣṇa is successful. Developing the heart’s eyes and seeing Kṛṣṇa, such a soul abandons all delusions."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["    vṛndāvana-keli chatur vanamālī","tribhaṅga-bhaṅgimā-rūpa    vaṁśī-dhārī aparūpa","    rasamaya nidhi, guṇa-śālī"],"translation":["Kṛṣṇa is expert at play in Vṛndāvan. He wears a forest garland, poses bent in three places, and plays the flute perfectly. He is a reservoir of rasa and possesses all qualities."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["varṇa nava jaladhara    śire śikhi-pichchha-vara","    alakā tilaka śobhā pāya","paridhāne pīta-vāsa    vadane madhura hāsa","    hena rūpa jagat mātāya"],"translation":["His complexion is the colour of a fresh rain cloud. His forehead is adorned with tilak, curling locks, and a fine peacock feather. He wears yellow garments and a sweet smile on His face. His form enchants the world."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["indra-nīla jini    kṛṣṇa-rūpa-khāni","    heriyā kadamba-mūle","mana uchāṭana    nā chale charaṇa","    saṁsāra gelāma bhule"],"translation":["Beholding Kṛṣṇa’s form, which surpasses the beauty of a sapphire, beneath a kadamba, my heart was overwhelmed. My feet could not move. I forgot the world."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["    (sakhī he) sudhāmaya se rūpa mādhurī","dekhile nayana    haya achetana","    jhare premamaya vāri"],"translation":["O friend! When I saw the beauty of Kṛṣṇa’s nectarean form, I fainted and shed tears of divine love."],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["kibā chūḍā śire    kibā vaṁśī kare","    kibā se tribhaṅga ṭhāma","charaṇa-kamale    amiyā uchhale","    tāhāte nūpura dāma"],"translation":["What a crown on His head! What a flute in His hand! What a threefold pose! Nectar surged from His lotus feet, which were adorned with tinkling anklets."],"isLong":false},{"number":"7","text":["sadā āśā kari    bhṛṅga-rūpa dhari","    charaṇa-kamale sthāna","anāyāse pāi    kṛṣṇa-guṇa gāi","    āra nā bhajiba āna"],"translation":["I eternally desire to take the form of a bee, easily attain a place at Kṛṣṇa’s lotus feet, and sing His glories. I will never serve anyone else."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/bharatimaharaj/govinda-maharaj-janamasaphala","personSlug":"srila-b-s-govinda-dev-goswami-maharaj"},{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/janama-saphala-tara","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":"https://telegra.ph/Rūpa-Kīrtan-02-22"},"head":{"canonical":"/en-pe/janama-saphala-tara-krishna-darashiana-jara/","description":"Rūpa-Kīrtan — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Pocket Kirtan Guide.","title":"Rūpa-Kīrtan. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-pe","slug":"janama-saphala-tara-krishna-darashiana-jara"}}